#: .\templates\index.html:577
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    My mission has always been to fill the gaps my community "
"faces day to day — gaps in education, in\n"
"                    leadership, in opportunity. Where some see problems, I "
"see possibilities. Entrepreneurs are best\n"
"                    positioned to solve community challenges because they "
"are trained to recognize problems not as\n"
"                    obstacles, but as opportunities for innovation. Once "
"equipped with the right knowledge and global\n"
"                    perspective, they can bring the world back into their "
"communities — inspiring, motivating, and\n"
"                    driving real change.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    My mission has always been to fill the gaps my community "
"faces day to day — gaps in education, in\n"
"                    leadership, in opportunity. Where some see problems, I "
"see possibilities. Entrepreneurs are best\n"
"                    positioned to solve community challenges because they "
"are trained to recognize problems not as\n"
"                    obstacles, but as opportunities for innovation. Once "
"equipped with the right knowledge and global\n"
"                    perspective, they can bring the world back into their "
"communities — inspiring, motivating, and\n"
"                    driving real change.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:599
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    In 2020, I established Big Ben Education Hub with a bold "
"vision: to give young people access to\n"
"                    quality education and the confidence to participate in "
"shaping their futures. Despite the challenges\n"
"                    of the time, within the very first year we welcomed over "
"400 students. This success demonstrated\n"
"                    not only the demand for such a space, but also the power "
"of education as a springboard for\n"
"                    transformation.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    In 2020, I established Big Ben Education Hub with a bold "
"vision: to give young people access to\n"
"                    quality education and the confidence to participate in "
"shaping their futures. Despite the challenges\n"
"                    of the time, within the very first year we welcomed over "
"400 students. This success demonstrated\n"
"                    not only the demand for such a space, but also the power "
"of education as a springboard for\n"
"                    transformation.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:618
msgid "Scaling Impact: EU Project in Fergana Valley "
msgstr "Scaling Impact: EU Project in Fergana Valley"

#: .\templates\index.html:620
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    Soon after, I was invited to serve as Project Manager "
"for one of the largest EU-funded initiatives in\n"
"                    Uzbekistan’s Fergana Valley. With a budget of €329,000, "
"my role was to design and deliver 12\n"
"                    youth-led mini-projects across Andijan, Asaka, and seven "
"neighborhoods. For two years, I worked\n"
"                    closely with young leaders, training them to engage in "
"local decision-making and ensuring their\n"
"                    voices were heard. Watching these young people grow into "
"active changemakers convinced me\n"
"                    that empowered communities are built by empowered "
"individuals.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    Soon after, I was invited to serve as Project Manager "
"for one of the largest EU-funded initiatives in\n"
"                    Uzbekistan’s Fergana Valley. With a budget of €329,000, "
"my role was to design and deliver 12\n"
"                    youth-led mini-projects across Andijan, Asaka, and seven "
"neighborhoods. For two years, I worked\n"
"                    closely with young leaders, training them to engage in "
"local decision-making and ensuring their\n"
"                    voices were heard. Watching these young people grow into "
"active changemakers convinced me\n"
"                    that empowered communities are built by empowered "
"individuals.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:641
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    In 2022, I was selected for the Uzbekistan Business "
"Leaders (UBL) Program, funded by the\n"
"                    American Councils. Out of 300 applicants, I was chosen "
"as one of the finalists. This fellowship took\n"
"                    me to Austin, Texas, where I immersed myself in "
"entrepreneurial sessions at the University of\n"
"                    Texas. I saw firsthand how American entrepreneurs "
"innovate, collaborate, and solve problems at\n"
"                    scale. Upon returning, I launched the Andijan Business "
"Club, gathering over 60 entrepreneurs.\n"
"                    Together with local universities, we created a platform "
"where business leaders shared real-life\n"
"                    cases with students, while identifying and nurturing new "
"talent. This became a powerful bridge\n"
"                    between education and entrepreneurship.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    In 2022, I was selected for the Uzbekistan Business "
"Leaders (UBL) Program, funded by the\n"
"                    American Councils. Out of 300 applicants, I was chosen "
"as one of the finalists. This fellowship took\n"
"                    me to Austin, Texas, where I immersed myself in "
"entrepreneurial sessions at the University of\n"
"                    Texas. I saw firsthand how American entrepreneurs "
"innovate, collaborate, and solve problems at\n"
"                    scale. Upon returning, I launched the Andijan Business "
"Club, gathering over 60 entrepreneurs.\n"
"                    Together with local universities, we created a platform "
"where business leaders shared real-life\n"
"                    cases with students, while identifying and nurturing new "
"talent. This became a powerful bridge\n"
"                    between education and entrepreneurship.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:665
#, python-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    In 2023, I was awarded the Chevening Scholarship — one "
"of the most prestigious UK Government\n"
"                    awards. Only 1–2%% of all applicants worldwide succeed, "
"and I was honored to be among them.\n"
"                    Through Chevening, I completed my Master’s in "
"Entrepreneurship, Innovation, and Enterprise\n"
"                    Development in London (2023–2024). But my ambition was "
"never just to study — I wanted to act.\n"
"                    Returning to Uzbekistan, I opened the second branch of "
"Big Ben Education Hub, which became\n"
"                    more than a learning center. It is now a hybrid "
"ecosystem: - A coworking space for entrepreneurs \n"
"                    A training hub for English teachers to grow skills and "
"income - A networking zone for students and\n"
"                    business leaders to connect, collaborate, and create "
"opportunities together This reflects my\n"
"                    philosophy: education and entrepreneurship together are "
"the engines of social change.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    In 2023, I was awarded the Chevening Scholarship — one "
"of the most prestigious UK Government\n"
"                    awards. Only 1–2%% of all applicants worldwide succeed, "
"and I was honored to be among them.\n"
"                    Through Chevening, I completed my Master’s in "
"Entrepreneurship, Innovation, and Enterprise\n"
"                    Development in London (2023–2024). But my ambition was "
"never just to study — I wanted to act.\n"
"                    Returning to Uzbekistan, I opened the second branch of "
"Big Ben Education Hub, which became\n"
"                    more than a learning center. It is now a hybrid "
"ecosystem: - A coworking space for entrepreneurs \n"
"                    A training hub for English teachers to grow skills and "
"income - A networking zone for students and\n"
"                    business leaders to connect, collaborate, and create "
"opportunities together This reflects my\n"
"                    philosophy: education and entrepreneurship together are "
"the engines of social change.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:690
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    Inspired by my U.S. experience, I launched the Andijan "
"Business Leaders Program. Unlike\n"
"                    programs that target students alone, this initiative "
"empowers young entrepreneurs who each\n"
"                    employ 40+ people across industries such as "
"pharmaceuticals, textiles, IT, hospitality, education,\n"
"                    furniture, and real estate. - In 2024 and 2025, I led 20 "
"entrepreneurs on 10-day leadership journeys\n"
"                    in London. These were not just trips — they were "
"accelerators. Participants returned with global\n"
"                    best practices, stronger networks, and fresh strategies "
"to apply in their businesses and\n"
"                    communities. - In 2026, I will take 10 outstanding "
"entrepreneurs to the United States, connecting\n"
"                    Andijan’s leaders with global markets and networks. This "
"multiplies their ability to improve\n"
"                    industries, generate jobs, and solve pressing community "
"challenges.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                    Inspired by my U.S. experience, I launched the Andijan "
"Business Leaders Program. Unlike\n"
"                    programs that target students alone, this initiative "
"empowers young entrepreneurs who each\n"
"                    employ 40+ people across industries such as "
"pharmaceuticals, textiles, IT, hospitality, education,\n"
"                    furniture, and real estate. - In 2024 and 2025, I led 20 "
"entrepreneurs on 10-day leadership journeys\n"
"                    in London. These were not just trips — they were "
"accelerators. Participants returned with global\n"
"                    best practices, stronger networks, and fresh strategies "
"to apply in their businesses and\n"
"                    communities. - In 2026, I will take 10 outstanding "
"entrepreneurs to the United States, connecting\n"
"                    Andijan’s leaders with global markets and networks. This "
"multiplies their ability to improve\n"
"                    industries, generate jobs, and solve pressing community "
"challenges.\n"
"                    "

#: .\templates\index.html:715
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    Real change does not happen overnight. It requires "
"influence, impact, and persistence. 1. Influence\n"
"                    minds with education and exposure. 2. Affect systems "
"through leadership and collaboration. 3.\n"
"                    Create impact that transforms communities and "
"industries. Every project I lead — in education,\n"
"                    entrepreneurship, or leadership development — follows "
"this process. By educating and\n"
"                    empowering entrepreneurs, I am building the capacity of "
"those who can solve the most pressing\n"
"                    challenges our communities face. I believe the future of "
"Andijan, and Uzbekistan as a whole, lies in\n"
"                    its entrepreneurs — educated, globally aware, and "
"locally committed. They are the ones who will\n"
"                    see every problem as an opportunity and transform "
"challenges into stepping stones toward\n"
"                    progress.\n"
"                    "
